5.5 Submission stage rules (enforced by DB; mirror them in the UI)
applied → recruiter_review | rejected | withdrawn
recruiter_review → client_review | rejected | withdrawn     (client_review = "Share with client")
client_review → interviewing | rejected | withdrawn
interviewing → offered | rejected | withdrawn
offered → offer_accepted | offer_declined | withdrawn
offer_accepted → onboarded | withdrawn
HQ: any allowed transition.
Client: client_review→interviewing/rejected, interviewing→offered/rejected.
Vendor (own submissions) and candidate (own application): withdraw only.
Only show buttons the current user can actually use for the current stage.
5.6 Error handling (src/lib/errors.ts)
Map Supabase/Postgres errors to friendly messages:

code 42501 or message starting FORBIDDEN → "You don't have permission to do this."
RLS violation ("row-level security") → "This action isn't allowed for your role."
23505 unique → "This already exists."
23514 check → show the field-level validation message.
"Invalid transition" / "A reason is required" → show as is.
RPC {status:'duplicate'} → a non-error Duplicate detected dialog that explains "HireNest has been notified to review ownership. Nothing was merged." Never show raw SQL or stack traces. Log only error codes, never payloads.
