7. END-TO-END FLOWS TO IMPLEMENT AND VERIFY
A. Requirement → Candidates: client creates draft → submits for approval → HQ opens (matches compute automatically) → HQ shares with vendors and/or makes it public → HQ reviews the ranked matches with evidence → explicit submit/shortlist → submission + history + audit.
B. Candidate → Requirements: candidate created/updated → matches recompute automatically → Potential Matches shown → explicit apply (candidate) or submit (vendor/HQ). Matching alone never creates a transaction.
C. Vendor candidate: vendor sees a shared requirement → acknowledges → adds a candidate (hash + duplicate check) → reviews match evidence → submits → HQ sees vendor name + source → HQ shares with client → client reviews → interviews and statuses update the same submission.
D. Direct candidate: register → profile + resume → sees eligible jobs → match evidence → apply → Admin sees "Direct applicant / Applied" with no vendor → recruiter review → client review → decision.
E. AI screening interview: Phase 2. Show a disabled "AI screening (coming soon, Ollama)" card on the submission detail. Do not simulate it.
F. Admin oversight: dashboard → drill into any entity → filter by source / vendor / client / status → inspect audit → act → notification reaches the right workspace.
G. Ratings: interview completed → client sees "Feedback pending" → submits the interview feedback form → submits the candidate quality form → admin reviews and optionally shares with the vendor → vendor sees shared feedback → may dispute → admin resolves → vendor scores update.
8. RATING SYSTEM (new feature, build fully)
8.1 Client interview feedback form (after each round)
Interview stage: read-only from the interview (round_type: Initial Screening / Technical Round / Managerial Round / Final Round)
Job-related skill assessment: 1–5 (1 = Poor · 5 = Excellent), as a 5-segment RatingInput with labels
Communication and clarity: 1–5
Overall interview rating: 1–5
Interview decision: Advance to next round / Hold for review / Reject / Additional assessment required (advance|hold|reject|additional_assessment)
Feedback and evidence: feedback (required, min 10 chars, placeholder with a good example), evidence (optional: specific answers or observations)
Submit → insert into interview_feedback. Show "Feedback is final and visible to HireNest. It is shared with the vendor only if HireNest approves." If the decision is Reject, offer (do not force) moving the submission to rejected via transition_submission with a reason.
8.2 Candidate quality rating (client, per submission, once per rater)
Six 1–5 ratings: JD skill alignment, Relevant experience, Resume accuracy & completeness, Communication & professionalism, Interview readiness, Overall candidate suitability + comments → candidate_quality_feedback. Linked to the specific candidate + requirement submission.

8.3 Vendor submission-timing metrics (computed by DB)
Response speed (avg hours share → acknowledge), submission turnaround (avg hours share → first valid submission), SLA compliance (first valid submission ≤ due_at), consistency (SLA compliance over the last 90 days).

