9. UI / UX STANDARDS
Design language: clean enterprise SaaS. Neutral slate greys, one brand colour (indigo-600), and semantic colours for status (green = on time / advance, amber = pending / hold, red = late / reject). Inter font, 14px base, 8px spacing grid, rounded-lg cards, subtle borders instead of heavy shadows. Light and dark mode.
Consistent page anatomy: page title + one-line description + primary action (top right) → filter bar → content → pagination.
Every async view has four states: loading (skeletons, not spinners on full pages), empty (icon + what it means + next action), error (friendly message + Retry), and success.
Badges: SourceBadge (Vendor · / Direct applicant / HireNest sourced), StageBadge (one colour per stage), SlaBadge, ScoreBar (0–100 with the number), NotEnoughData.
Match evidence panel: score bar, skill score, experience score + note, matched skills (green chips), unproven skills (grey dashed chips, tooltip "Not found on profile; not proof the skill is missing"), engine version + calculated time, and the override banner if any.
Forms: inline zod errors, disabled submit while pending, toast on success, no data loss on error.
Tables: sticky header, sortable where the query supports it, row click → detail, empty filter result state with "Clear filters".
Accessibility: keyboard navigable, visible focus ring, aria labels on icon buttons, colour never the only signal, WCAG AA contrast.
Responsive: sidebar collapses to a drawer under 1024px. Tables become stacked cards under 640px.
Copy: plain, professional. Use "Requirement" (not "Job") in HQ/client/vendor views and "Job" in the candidate view.
10. SECURITY CHECKLIST (the UI must not undermine the DB)
Only the anon key in the browser. Read env from import.meta.env. Show a setup screen if it's missing.
Never pass vendor_org_id, source, submitted_by, rated_by or role from the client; the DB sets them.
Resume files: private bucket, signed URLs (5 min), sanitize file names, enforce type and size before upload.
Do not cache PII in localStorage. TanStack Query cache is in memory only. Clear it on sign-out.
Mask contact details in lists (e.g. ra***@gmail.com, +91 ******3210); reveal on the detail page only for allowed roles.
No dangerouslySetInnerHTML. Render JD text as plain text with line breaks.
Rate-limit UI actions (disable buttons while pending) to avoid duplicate RPC calls.
