12. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (demonstrate each)
Client A creates a requirement; Client B cannot see it.
A vendor sees only requirements shared with it, and never the client budget or margin.
A vendor-uploaded candidate appears in Admin with the correct vendor name and source.
A direct candidate appears in Admin as "Direct applicant" with no vendor.
A potential match does not create an application; explicit apply does.
Both matching directions work, filtered by role.
A duplicate candidate or submission shows the duplicate dialog, creates an admin flag and never merges.
Scores and evidence come from candidate_matches, never computed or mocked in the UI.
Recruiter override changes the displayed score and shows the reason.
Client feedback is not visible to the vendor until admin approval.
Vendor scores show "Not enough data" below the minimum sample size and "Pending approval" until weights are approved.
Disputes can be raised (vendor_admin) and resolved (admin); upheld feedback leaves the score.
Every stage change appears in the timeline with actor, time and reason.
Pending and suspended users can't reach any workspace.
Every list is paginated and has loading, empty and error states.
npm run build and npm run lint pass with zero TypeScript errors.
